WEBVTT

00:00.930 --> 00:02.920
<i>(Isn't that maybe how love's defined?)</i>

00:02.920 --> 00:04.650
<i>Wow! A gift for you!</i>

00:04.650 --> 00:06.520
<i>(So, isn't that true love defined?)</i>

00:11.930 --> 00:13.720
<i>Nothing happening,</i>

00:13.720 --> 00:15.910
<i>every day feels the same</i>

00:15.910 --> 00:17.320
<i>Over and over, just</i>

00:17.320 --> 00:19.400
<i>waiting for time to pass</i>

00:19.400 --> 00:21.420
<i>When I'm with you,</i>

00:21.420 --> 00:22.620
<i>I can feel</i>

00:22.620 --> 00:24.750
<i>something so special,</i>

00:24.750 --> 00:27.880
<i>and I want to make it real</i>

00:27.880 --> 00:30.380
<i>Look, I'm really grateful every day, but you know</i>

00:30.380 --> 00:32.270
<i>I feel like I'm not doing enough in return</i>

00:32.270 --> 00:33.920
<i>"I was just feeling like it.</i>

00:33.920 --> 00:35.720
<i>No real meaning or reason why."</i>

00:35.720 --> 00:40.110
<i>Stop complaining and just take it already!</i>

00:39.080 --> 00:40.960
<i>(Isn't that maybe how love's defined?)</i>

00:40.960 --> 00:43.520
<i>Yeah, there's no way that's how it goes!</i>

00:42.680 --> 00:44.350
<i>(So, isn't that true love defined?)</i>

00:44.350 --> 00:46.360
<i>Whoa oh oh oh oh</i>

00:46.360 --> 00:48.810
<i>An angel just landed</i>

00:48.810 --> 00:50.700
<i>Right in front of me</i>

00:50.700 --> 00:52.320
<i>With a smile that looked</i>

00:52.320 --> 00:53.990
<i>Like her wings spreading open</i>

00:53.990 --> 00:55.950
<i>Hey, that's against all the rules</i>

00:55.950 --> 00:57.360
<i>You look so happy</i>

00:57.360 --> 00:59.290
<i>Wipe off that look</i>

00:59.290 --> 01:01.180
<i>Before my mind goes blank</i>

01:01.180 --> 01:03.020
<i>If you keep this up,</i>

01:03.020 --> 01:05.640
<i>You're gonna spoil me rotten</i>

01:06.460 --> 01:09.760
<i>Come on, you gotta do something about this</i>

01:08.220 --> 01:10.480
<i>So, let's get started</i>

01:10.480 --> 01:11.610
<i>I want to know</i>

01:11.610 --> 01:13.640
<i>A lot more about</i>

01:13.640 --> 01:15.680
<i>The world you live in</i>

01:15.680 --> 01:17.880
<i>So, let's get started</i>

01:17.880 --> 01:18.910
<i>I want to laugh</i>

01:18.910 --> 01:20.890
<i>A lot more with you</i>

01:20.890 --> 01:23.050
<i>In the world you live in</i>

01:22.350 --> 01:26.640
The Angel Next Door
Spoils Me Rotten

01:23.050 --> 01:25.020
<i>I want to know more</i>

01:25.020 --> 01:27.690
<i>I want to laugh more</i>

01:31.620 --> 01:35.240
Amane-kun, I see someone very special in you.

01:35.900 --> 01:37.240
Someone very cute.

01:46.560 --> 01:50.250
The next time you say something like that, 
I'll shut your mouth without the hand.

02:05.500 --> 02:06.630
Why?

02:07.810 --> 02:12.820
Say Goodbye to My Cowardice

02:13.830 --> 02:17.130
Hey, hey! What are you doing 
for sports day, Mahirun?

02:17.130 --> 02:21.820
I still haven't decided, 
but the scavenger race does look fun.

02:22.330 --> 02:24.700
Oh, it'll be a blast!

02:24.700 --> 02:28.250
After all, I'm on the event committee,
 and I'm in charge of that one.

02:28.660 --> 02:30.880
It sounds like a lot of fun, then.

02:30.880 --> 02:32.380
Yo, Amane.

02:32.380 --> 02:33.090
Yo.

02:33.680 --> 02:35.130
Morning, Fujimiya.

02:35.130 --> 02:35.840
Morning.

02:37.300 --> 02:38.600
Morning, Amane!

02:38.600 --> 02:39.970
Yeah. Morning.

02:48.520 --> 02:50.940
<b>Cafeteria</b>

02:52.020 --> 02:54.970
Hey, Amane, are you two fighting or something?

02:54.970 --> 02:56.780
Huh? You're fighting, Fujimiya?

02:57.240 --> 03:00.280
No, we aren't exactly fighting.

03:00.280 --> 03:03.270
But it's, well, I don't know...

03:03.270 --> 03:05.030
Some stuff just happened.

03:08.560 --> 03:11.920
Just some stuff between us. 
We're kind of keeping our distance.

03:12.360 --> 03:15.820
Come on, man. How long are you 
gonna mope around like that?

03:15.820 --> 03:16.920
Shut up.

03:17.240 --> 03:20.380
Well, Fujimiya does seem 
like the cautious type.

03:20.380 --> 03:23.590
I doubt he'll make a move 
until he knows the coast is clear.

03:23.590 --> 03:25.680
Yeah, and that's what I call moping around.

03:27.500 --> 03:31.990
If I knew she liked me... if I could be 
more confident, it would be easier.

03:32.720 --> 03:36.230
I mean, if I were better looking, 
I could be more confident that she likes me.

03:37.060 --> 03:40.820
You're really passive despite
 being such a quality catch.

03:41.500 --> 03:44.530
Says the guy who's pretty 
much the top-quality catch.

03:45.340 --> 03:50.290
Anyway, even with this going on, 
I'm still moving things along at my own pace.

03:50.820 --> 03:52.540
Don't try to rush me, okay?

03:53.360 --> 03:56.420
I mean, that's fine if you say so, Fujimiya.

03:56.420 --> 03:58.470
But we're a little impatient over here.

03:58.470 --> 03:59.420
Totally.

03:59.420 --> 04:02.680
When's the next meeting of 
the Kick-Amane-in-the-Pants Committee?

04:03.980 --> 04:05.680
What the hell are you guys plotting?

04:06.220 --> 04:08.310
Hey, this is our way of rooting for you.

04:26.500 --> 04:32.330
Um, I want to apologize for yesterday.
 For leaving before dinner.

04:33.000 --> 04:36.750
It's... fine. I'm not worried about it.

04:45.950 --> 04:49.720
I mean... about yesterday, you know...

04:52.050 --> 04:54.440
Why did you do that, Mahiru?

04:56.320 --> 05:00.320
I guess I got carried away. 
Or I wanted to get back at you.

05:00.970 --> 05:02.690
Get back at me?

05:02.690 --> 05:06.570
Because you... did it too, right?

05:06.980 --> 05:07.950
Wait, no...

05:07.950 --> 05:11.490
Well, I guess I kind of did.

05:11.490 --> 05:14.410
So don't I also have the right to?

05:14.410 --> 05:16.420
That isn't the point.

05:16.880 --> 05:17.880
I mean...

05:19.600 --> 05:21.010
What is it?

05:22.340 --> 05:23.630
Never mind.

05:26.640 --> 05:28.010
I'm on red!

05:29.960 --> 05:32.680
Oh, right. Itsuki is on white.

05:30.680 --> 05:32.680
<b>Second Year Red/White Team Assignments</b>

05:30.680 --> 05:32.680
<b>Red {赤}</b>

05:30.680 --> 05:32.680
<b>White {白}</b>

05:33.080 --> 05:35.910
Why couldn't we get the teams 
that matched our names?

05:35.310 --> 05:39.670
Shirakawa

05:35.310 --> 05:39.670
Akazawa

05:35.910 --> 05:37.780
Either way, you'd still be competing.

05:37.780 --> 05:38.780
<i>Let's share the win!</i>

05:38.780 --> 05:40.060
<i>Leave it to me!</i>

05:41.140 --> 05:43.500
Is that true? This is tragic!

05:43.500 --> 05:46.840
Bitter rivals drawn to each another 
in a forbidden love!

05:46.840 --> 05:48.240
Ugh. Whatever.

05:48.800 --> 05:50.740
What events are you in, Amane?

05:51.840 --> 05:53.940
What were the options again?

06:03.780 --> 06:07.220
What sports day events 
did you sign up for, Mahiru?

06:09.550 --> 06:12.300
I picked the relay and the scavenger race.

06:12.300 --> 06:13.680
Oh, we're together, then.

06:13.960 --> 06:16.270
I picked the bag toss and the scavenger race.

06:17.460 --> 06:18.520
Here you go.

06:18.520 --> 06:19.850
Yeah. Thank you.

06:20.330 --> 06:22.900
Avoiding a workout at all costs, are you?

06:22.900 --> 06:25.460
I'm not very athletic anyway.

06:25.460 --> 06:29.850
Weren't your P.E. grades pretty 
average, Amane-kun?

06:29.850 --> 06:31.670
Yeah, unfortunately.

06:40.050 --> 06:43.630
Be honest with me. 
You hate sports day, don't you?

06:43.630 --> 06:49.540
Yeah. I don't exactly hate exercise, 
I just hate being forced to do it.

06:50.210 --> 06:56.180
I can't disagree with that. 
I don't really like to be forced, either.

06:56.540 --> 07:01.020
Right? So, you know, 
I just play along and get it over with.

07:02.510 --> 07:05.940
I guess I won't get to see you 
in all your athletic glory.

07:05.940 --> 07:07.150
Who knows?

07:07.150 --> 07:10.530
I might really shine in the bag toss.

07:11.300 --> 07:12.910
Sure, it could happen.

07:13.330 --> 07:16.080
It's still a boring event.
I won't stand out either way.

07:16.440 --> 07:18.560
You still have to try your best, though.

07:19.700 --> 07:21.120
Yeah, I'll do all right.

07:21.610 --> 07:22.850
Boy...

07:31.870 --> 07:32.640
Huh?

07:38.240 --> 07:40.870
This is the really good stuff, isn't it?

07:40.870 --> 07:41.690
You can tell?

07:41.990 --> 07:44.630
Well, I could tell from the container.

07:45.050 --> 07:46.660
But it's better than I expected.

07:46.660 --> 07:48.150
Oh, yeah? Here.

07:53.890 --> 07:57.080
<i>Oh, no! I did it again without thinking.</i>

07:57.610 --> 07:59.830
Mahiru, you can have the rest.

08:02.530 --> 08:05.920
I'm making coffee, so I'm good.

08:05.920 --> 08:07.330
It's yours.

08:14.000 --> 08:17.640
<i>I was trying to keep some distance between us,</i>

08:18.500 --> 08:20.310
<i>but it never lasts.</i>

08:20.310 --> 08:22.560
<b>Seijo High School</b>

08:20.310 --> 08:22.560
<b>41st Annual</b>

08:20.310 --> 08:22.560
<b>Sports Day</b>

08:22.560 --> 08:23.700
Go!

08:22.560 --> 08:24.310
Go, white!

08:24.310 --> 08:26.060
Don't let them win, red!

08:27.630 --> 08:28.860
I'm pooped.

08:28.860 --> 08:30.060
Me, too, man.

08:30.060 --> 08:31.760
I can barely move.

08:32.540 --> 08:34.680
You don't seem to hate this, Fujimiya.

08:35.070 --> 08:36.450
I kind of thought you would.

08:36.970 --> 08:39.120
Well, I got the events I wanted.

08:39.120 --> 08:43.460
And it does give us some time off, 
so I guess it isn't too bad.

08:43.460 --> 08:48.140
But why is Chitose in the relay race 
instead of someone from the track club?

08:48.140 --> 08:49.290
Is she that fast?

08:49.290 --> 08:51.550
Yeah. Shirakawa-san is really fast.

08:52.260 --> 08:54.680
In middle school, she was 
the ace of the track team.

08:55.020 --> 08:56.770
What? Seriously?

08:56.770 --> 08:57.430
Yeah.

08:57.960 --> 09:00.260
She never joined in high school, though.

09:01.970 --> 09:04.770
She didn't want to deal with drama 
from her senpai in the club.

09:05.160 --> 09:08.270
I guess it's funny that she expected drama.

09:08.270 --> 09:12.760
Yeah, well... there's actually 
a reason for that.

09:13.440 --> 09:16.660
I think she'd had enough. 
She was just kind of tired.

09:16.970 --> 09:18.020
Tired of what?

09:18.900 --> 09:22.740
A lot of stuff went on before she 
started going out with Itsuki.

09:22.740 --> 09:24.710
It's basically, like...

09:25.340 --> 09:28.460
One of her senpai in track liked Itsuki.

09:29.030 --> 09:32.550
And she also got better times 
than that senpai, so...

09:32.930 --> 09:34.600
I could have guessed.

09:34.600 --> 09:38.780
Chi! You're awesome! You did great!

09:38.780 --> 09:39.760
Ikkun!

09:42.270 --> 09:43.580
I'm back!

09:43.580 --> 09:44.490
Did you see?

09:44.490 --> 09:47.100
We did, we did! You were really fast!

09:47.100 --> 09:48.770
Yay! Thanks!

09:49.860 --> 09:52.060
I guess I'd better get ready.

09:52.060 --> 09:54.310
Oh. The scavenger race, right?

09:54.310 --> 09:54.990
Yeah.

09:55.450 --> 09:56.420
Amanay!

09:56.420 --> 09:57.070
Huh?

09:57.520 --> 10:00.390
I'm in charge of the scavenger race!

10:00.390 --> 10:01.890
I promise it won't disappoint!

10:02.420 --> 10:03.950
Good luck, okay?

10:05.500 --> 10:07.910
I have nothing but bad feelings about this.

10:08.360 --> 10:12.590
Participating athletes, 
please line up in order at the start line.

10:14.380 --> 10:17.410
On your mark, get set...

10:26.550 --> 10:29.670
Fujimiya-san, you match what's on my card.

10:29.670 --> 10:32.950
Once you find what you need, 
will you come with me?

10:32.950 --> 10:34.090
Huh? I do?

10:34.090 --> 10:34.980
Yes.

10:39.030 --> 10:41.260
<i>I won't let her off easy this time.</i>

10:41.260 --> 10:43.500
By the way, what are you looking for?

10:43.500 --> 10:44.580
It's a secret.

10:45.010 --> 10:47.800
You match what I need, too, 
so let's head for the finish line.

10:48.250 --> 10:51.120
What were you searching for, Fujimiya-san?

10:51.120 --> 10:52.580
It's a secret.

10:54.140 --> 10:57.300
I suppose it is. It'll be fun to 
find out at the finish line.

10:57.840 --> 10:58.760
Hey!

11:00.720 --> 11:03.910
Huh? Is Shiina-san holding that guy's hand?

11:03.910 --> 11:06.350
I'm sure it just means he matches her list.

11:06.350 --> 11:09.440
Fujimiya, you son of a—! 
Trade places with me!

11:12.200 --> 11:15.180
Oh, wow! Did they reach the goal together?

11:15.180 --> 11:18.400
And I believe they're both runners 
in the scavenger race!

11:18.730 --> 11:21.110
We matched each other's item.

11:21.110 --> 11:25.340
Aha. Then let's read what you got. 
Who goes first?

11:25.340 --> 11:27.540
Fujimiya-san, would you go first?

11:27.960 --> 11:28.950
Sure.

11:29.560 --> 11:33.670
I'll read the cards now. 
The first runner from the red team has...

11:34.070 --> 11:36.700
"Someone I Think Is Beautiful." That's right!

11:34.130 --> 11:39.670
Someone I Think Is Beautiful

11:36.700 --> 11:39.670
No question, this one is a winner!

11:40.340 --> 11:42.640
And next up is Shiina-san.

11:44.160 --> 11:44.930
Oh.

11:49.390 --> 11:52.540
<i>What item did she think I matched, anyway?</i>

11:53.510 --> 11:59.440
Um, finishing at the same time, 
the runner from the white team has...

11:59.440 --> 12:01.950
Someone Very Dear to Me

11:59.950 --> 12:01.950
"Someone Very Dear to Me!" Yes!

12:18.000 --> 12:22.970
The Angel Next Door
Spoils Me Rotten

12:23.580 --> 12:25.300
The hell is going on, Fujimiya?!

12:25.630 --> 12:28.610
Why are you with Shiina-san? 
And this "very dear" crap?

12:28.610 --> 12:29.940
Yeah, since when?

12:29.940 --> 12:31.850
You don't have anything in common!

12:32.340 --> 12:35.950
What is it? What the hell 
does Shiina-san see in you?!

12:35.950 --> 12:37.480
It doesn't make any sense!

12:38.220 --> 12:41.280
I can't answer when you're all asking at once.

12:41.280 --> 12:43.280
At least ask me one at a time.

12:43.990 --> 12:47.420
How long have you and Shiina-san been close?

12:47.420 --> 12:48.330
Since last year.

12:48.430 --> 12:49.410
Huh?

12:49.410 --> 12:55.710
You mean the guy Shiina-san was with
 during New Year's and Golden Week was...?

12:56.780 --> 12:58.000
That would be me.

12:58.000 --> 12:58.880
Huh?

12:58.880 --> 13:00.910
H-How did you get to know her?

13:00.910 --> 13:03.170
You guys have basically nothing in common!

13:03.550 --> 13:06.110
And you always acted like strangers!

13:06.110 --> 13:08.180
We live near each other. That's how.

13:08.560 --> 13:13.310
And we acted like strangers because 
we knew you guys would freak out like this.

13:14.890 --> 13:16.700
It still doesn't make sense.

13:16.700 --> 13:22.230
Fujimiya, then are you... 
g-going out with Shiina-san?

13:26.090 --> 13:27.520
We do get along

13:27.520 --> 13:30.530
and I think it's fair to say we're 
very dear to each other,

13:30.530 --> 13:31.990
but we aren't going out.

13:33.060 --> 13:35.250
My own feelings are another issue.

13:35.500 --> 13:40.340
Yeah, right. You still acted like you 
didn't give a damn about our angel.

13:40.340 --> 13:42.440
I <i>don't</i> give a damn about your angel.

13:43.650 --> 13:47.760
The person I'm interested in is 
a real girl named Mahiru Shiina.

13:48.900 --> 13:51.810
Please don't bully him too much, okay?

13:52.110 --> 13:54.980
It's lunch break and he can't even eat.

13:54.980 --> 13:56.850
You're really making trouble for him.

13:56.850 --> 13:59.980
Shiina-san! Is Fujimiya 
the one who's "dear" to you?

14:01.200 --> 14:04.160
Yes, Amane-kun is very dear to me.

14:04.160 --> 14:08.240
So, does that mean, like, 
you <i>like</i> him or something?

14:08.780 --> 14:10.530
Supposing it does,

14:10.530 --> 14:13.240
is there something you want to say to me?

14:13.760 --> 14:16.140
Ah, well, it's just...

14:16.650 --> 14:20.500
If you had to like someone, 
why'd it have to be someone like Fujimiya?

14:21.610 --> 14:23.000
Someone <i>like</i> Fujimiya?

14:23.000 --> 14:24.750
Mahi— Um, Shiina!

14:25.230 --> 14:29.470
Yeah, he's so dull. It's weird that
 you'd go for a guy like that.

14:29.470 --> 14:31.260
There are way better guys out there.

14:31.700 --> 14:32.760
Oh, are there?

14:35.420 --> 14:39.270
So, in what way, exactly, is Amane-kun dull?

14:39.760 --> 14:41.780
Huh? Well...

14:41.780 --> 14:42.990
I mean, it's obvious.

14:42.990 --> 14:46.530
Exactly what part of him is dull? 
Would you mind explaining that to me?

14:46.530 --> 14:50.280
H-His style and stuff. His looks.

14:50.280 --> 14:53.280
So you only care about
 people for their looks?

14:53.280 --> 14:55.040
N-No, it's just...

14:55.040 --> 14:57.380
You would only like someone 
for their appearance?

14:57.380 --> 15:00.590
You would choose a partner, 
someone you might spend a long time with,

15:00.590 --> 15:02.560
just based on the way she looks now?

15:02.560 --> 15:04.090
I-I mean...

15:04.090 --> 15:06.050
I think the real matter at issue here

15:06.050 --> 15:09.130
is that you are <i>wholly</i> 
unqualified to comment

15:09.130 --> 15:12.680
on who I choose to be with,
 for whatever reason.

15:17.940 --> 15:21.640
Oh, that might have been 
a little too harsh. I'm sorry.

15:22.530 --> 15:25.570
But allow me to correct 
what you were saying before.

15:26.260 --> 15:30.450
Amane is very cool 
and he's a very kind person.

15:30.830 --> 15:34.450
He has a calm, gentle way about him 
that I think is wonderful.

15:35.020 --> 15:38.290
He's a delightful individual who respects me

15:38.290 --> 15:41.050
and acts like a true gentleman.

15:41.800 --> 15:45.000
When things are difficult, 
he stands by my side.

15:45.000 --> 15:47.210
He's very thoughtful.

15:47.700 --> 15:53.720
At the very least, he doesn't insult 
others or judge their relationships.

15:54.420 --> 15:56.850
Was there anything else you wanted to say?

15:57.330 --> 15:59.920
N-No, there isn't.

16:01.060 --> 16:02.760
Sorry to bother you.

16:06.460 --> 16:09.360
Let's eat together, Amane-kun.

16:10.070 --> 16:10.920
Sure.

16:12.140 --> 16:21.250
One! Two! Three! Four! Five! Six!

16:20.140 --> 16:21.250
<i>I've got to tell her.</i>

16:21.250 --> 16:24.260
Seven! Eight!

16:22.820 --> 16:25.930
<i>When I get home, I'll tell her.</i>

16:44.330 --> 16:46.240
<i>I need to find the right words.</i>

17:02.630 --> 17:03.840
Amane-kun.

17:14.630 --> 17:20.700
I imagine you have a lot to say, 
and maybe a lot of questions for me.

17:21.170 --> 17:24.060
But would you let me say one thing first?

17:24.060 --> 17:25.600
S-Sure.

17:26.860 --> 17:28.590
I feel bad about cornering you

17:28.590 --> 17:34.760
and giving you a lot of attention 
that you probably didn't want.

17:35.270 --> 17:36.850
I'm truly sorry about that.

17:36.850 --> 17:37.740
Huh?

17:38.680 --> 17:42.490
You see, I knew that this would happen.

17:44.810 --> 17:49.600
Yeah, I could tell that you
 did it intentionally.

17:49.600 --> 17:50.500
Huh?

17:50.980 --> 17:52.530
And you aren't mad about it?

17:52.530 --> 17:54.020
No, I'm not mad.

17:54.020 --> 17:57.010
Really? That's a relief.

17:59.440 --> 18:01.260
Now, will you let <i>me</i> apologize?

18:01.810 --> 18:02.760
For what?

18:04.300 --> 18:05.690
I'm sorry I'm such a coward.

18:06.980 --> 18:10.520
I knew it, but I was too scared to act. 
I looked the other way.

18:10.910 --> 18:14.530
I pretended not to notice your feelings. 
I pretended not to see.

18:14.530 --> 18:15.280
I'm sorry.

18:21.280 --> 18:25.540
Then I think we're both guilty. 
I acted basically the same way.

18:26.190 --> 18:32.790
I wasn't able to make a move either until 
I was sure of your feelings for me.

18:33.840 --> 18:37.720
Didn't I tell you before? 
About how selfish I am.

18:38.260 --> 18:39.470
I'm not so sure.

18:44.730 --> 18:46.220
I think I'm the selfish one.

18:50.980 --> 18:52.810
Can I tell you how I feel?

18:55.850 --> 19:00.760
You know, I've never seriously 
fallen for anyone before.

19:01.530 --> 19:03.490
I mean, I never thought I would.

19:04.760 --> 19:06.490
I never even thought I could.

19:07.390 --> 19:09.500
Because of what happened in the past?

19:09.500 --> 19:11.000
Yeah, that's why.

19:11.670 --> 19:16.320
Because of that, I assumed I'd never 
be able to truly care about someone.

19:18.730 --> 19:21.760
I didn't expect to be proven wrong so easily.

19:22.520 --> 19:26.510
I guess people can change when they 
meet someone they really care about.

19:27.060 --> 19:30.890
You know, Mahiru, at first 
I didn't think you were charming at all.

19:31.580 --> 19:35.400
I know. You told me straight to my face.

19:36.180 --> 19:38.910
I'm sorry I acted that way. Honestly.

19:39.500 --> 19:45.530
When we first met, you were bossy, 
cold, and mean to me.

19:45.530 --> 19:48.430
So I thought things should stay 
purely give-and-take between us.

19:52.040 --> 19:55.790
Then at some point, 
I realized that wasn't enough.

19:58.200 --> 20:00.800
I wanted to know more about you.

20:01.460 --> 20:03.680
I wanted to touch you.

20:04.100 --> 20:07.560
I wanted to hold you 
deep in my heart and treasure you.

20:08.620 --> 20:10.620
I wanted <i>you</i>.

20:10.620 --> 20:12.310
I'd never felt this way before.

20:14.360 --> 20:15.060
I know.

20:15.690 --> 20:18.910
I held back. Thought I wasn't good enough.

20:19.320 --> 20:22.690
But then you told me I was.

20:22.690 --> 20:27.830
So instead of avoiding it, I tried to 
think of ways to bring us closer together.

20:28.860 --> 20:33.080
Of course, before I could make a move, 
you took the first step.

20:34.810 --> 20:37.090
I was holding back, too.

20:37.700 --> 20:43.220
I was worried someone else would see 
how cool you are and try to take you.

20:43.860 --> 20:48.610
So I was in a cold sweat over whether
 you'd ever start to like me.

20:48.610 --> 20:51.240
You're the only girl with
 tastes that unusual.

20:51.240 --> 20:53.450
There you go again.

20:58.610 --> 21:03.900
So, I'm going to work hard to 
make things less unusual for you.

21:03.900 --> 21:04.900
Huh?

21:05.300 --> 21:07.910
I don't want people to say
 you're strange for liking me.

21:08.510 --> 21:10.410
I'll become a better man.

21:11.160 --> 21:13.200
I'll climb to your level.

21:13.200 --> 21:16.670
Well, maybe not that high, but 
close enough to feel worthy of you.

21:20.170 --> 21:23.300
Mahiru, I care about you more than anyone.

21:28.610 --> 21:30.680
Will you go out with me?

21:31.610 --> 21:32.560
Mm-hmm.

21:39.100 --> 21:41.000
<i>I'll never let you go.</i>

21:42.040 --> 21:43.690
I want to make you happy.

21:44.570 --> 21:46.450
But you won't promise that?

21:46.910 --> 21:48.780
It's my one ambition.

21:48.780 --> 21:51.870
I want to bring you happiness 
with my own two hands.

21:53.100 --> 21:57.710
I give you my word. 
I will treasure you. Absolutely.

22:00.530 --> 22:01.090
Okay.

22:11.600 --> 22:18.270
<i>Your big, bright and sparkling eyes, 
they really flatter you</i>

22:18.270 --> 22:24.830
<i>And your playful voice 
and delicate hands also glow</i>

22:24.830 --> 22:31.420
<i>Though it's hard for you to smile, 
when one lights up your face,</i>

22:31.420 --> 22:38.760
<i>One more of the dreams I saw that day 
might just come true</i>

22:38.760 --> 22:46.010
<i>You see passing strangers come and go</i>

22:46.010 --> 22:51.070
<i>Why do you care about their happiness</i>

22:51.070 --> 22:57.320
<i>As much as you care about your own?</i>

22:57.320 --> 23:05.360
<i>It makes me really happy 
that you're someone that I got to know</i>

23:05.360 --> 23:10.510
<i>I can say that, and I'll do my best 
to keep you smiling</i>

23:10.510 --> 23:18.460
<i>Next year more, the next even more, 
my love will grow for you every way</i>

23:18.460 --> 23:24.060
<i>That's how much I know you fulfill me every day</i>

23:24.060 --> 23:30.910
<i>This message comes straight from me. 
I want you to know now that these words</i>

23:30.910 --> 23:34.720
<i>Are for you only</i>
